"""yan-v7 research challenger. Forecasts near-term bank receipts for both sides. Two elite styles, a compact opponent policy and replay-priced economic search.

Version-specific training and local evaluation: github.com/Zhaoyi-Yan/carbon, experiments/v7.
The following attribution describes the original competition agent.

Additional yan-v5 work: twenty replay-trained action heads, rival identification,
context-dependent style selection and 48-step cash evaluation.
Base code: yan-v1 (an adaptation of Claude's public claude-AlphaCarbon-Master3s2,
https://117.72.210.134/source/d679ed45ab595e8b7bb1ea51c3451154, which credits
Ryanx for the embedded engine). Search, belief tracker, features and engine are
unchanged from that file.

Changed: the policy network and critic were fine-tuned on 215 seats of public
replays (https://github.com/JUZI1/carbon-league-replays) played by the 11
strongest leaderboard strategies. Each teacher gets its own style embedding
(the network's existing style input); play uses the CarbonEdge_Apollo style.
Training used the 8 board symmetries, a KL penalty towards the original policy,
and critic distillation from the original critic. Sampling temperatures are
lowered to 0.4 for the less peaked fine-tuned policy.
"""
